From f31e8c8bb03975eae4be7772e83c115549b981fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erwin Jansen <jansene@google.com>
Date: Wed, 20 Aug 2025 22:56:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] build(glib): Add Windows support and fix Linux build

This change introduces the necessary configurations, source files, and
compatibility layers to enable building the glib library on Windows
using Bazel. Additionally, it resolves a compatibility issue with the
Linux toolchain.

To support Windows, the following was added:
- Platform-specific `config.h-windows` and `glibconfig.h.in-windows` to
  provide the correct build-time definitions.
- A minimal `gnulib` library to supply missing POSIX functions,
  notably for advanced printf functionality and math headers.
- A `dirent` library to provide the POSIX directory traversal API, which
  is absent on Windows.
- Bazel build logic to conditionally include Windows sources and link
  against required system libraries like `ws2_32.lib`.

The Linux build is fixed by disabling the `HAVE_LANGINFO_ABALTMON` and
`HAVE_LANGINFO_ALTMON` definitions, which were causing issues with the
aosp toolchain.
---
 BUILD.bazel                  |    2 +
 config.h-linux               |   10 +-
 config.h-windows             |  285 ++++
 glib/BUILD.bazel             |  374 +++++-
 glib/dirent/BUILD.bazel      |   13 +
 glib/glibconfig.h.in-windows |  219 +++
 gmodule/BUILD.bazel          |    2 +
 gnulib_math.h-windows        | 2452 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 8 files changed, 3351 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 config.h-windows
 create mode 100644 glib/dirent/BUILD.bazel
 create mode 100644 glib/glibconfig.h.in-windows
 create mode 100644 gnulib_math.h-windows

